"""How to repair: symptom-led repair procedures for the IT dashboard.

Written in our own words as practical field procedures, organised to match the CompTIA A+ 220-1201 (Core 1) troubleshooting domain
(5.1 motherboard, RAM, CPU and power; 5.2 drives and RAID; 5.3 video and displays; 5.4 mobile devices; 5.5 networks; 5.6 printers).
Each guide lists symptoms, likely causes from cheapest to check to most expensive, numbered steps, the tools you need, a safety note and when to stop."""
from __future__ import annotations

SAFETY = [
    "Power off and unplug before opening a desktop; for a laptop also remove the battery if it comes out, or disconnect the battery connector first.",
    "Discharge static: wear an ESD wrist strap clipped to bare case metal (or touch the bare chassis often), hold boards by the edges, and keep parts in antistatic bags.",
    "Never open a power supply or a CRT/older monitor, and never open a swollen or punctured battery. Stored charge can still hurt you after unplugging.",
    "Lift heavy gear with your legs, keep cables out of walkways, and wear gloves and eye protection when using compressed air, solvents or thermal cleaner. Dispose of batteries, toner and monitors at proper recycling points.",
    "Photograph or label cables and screws before removing them, and keep screws in a tray by location.",
]

METHOD = [
    ("Identify the problem", "Ask what changed, what it did and did not do, and when it last worked. Reproduce it. Back up important data before you change anything."),
    ("Make a theory", "List the likely causes from simplest and cheapest (cable, setting, power) to hardest (board, drive). Question the obvious first."),
    ("Test the theory", "Change one thing at a time and see what happens. If the theory is wrong, make a new one, or hand it to someone with more access."),
    ("Plan and fix", "Decide the fix, note the side effects, get approval if it changes the customer's system, then do it."),
    ("Verify and prevent", "Confirm the original symptom is gone and nothing else broke. Add the prevention step (update, clean, backup, surge protector)."),
    ("Write it up", "Record the symptom, cause, fix and time spent, so the next repair of this kind is faster and you can show the customer what you did."),
]

